    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d544">

                <pb facs="0564" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221 Dahl, Harold/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-11T13:00:00+00:00">October 11, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 11—12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of October 8, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d544-f1"/>
                    Harold Dahl. General Queipo de Llano informed me this morning that Dahl is <pb
                        facs="0565" n="553" xml:id="pg553"/> being exchanged and that the exchange
                    has probably already been effected. If it has not been concluded he said it will
                    take place immediately.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d544-f2"/> Repeated to Vigo and
                    Ambassador Bowers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d544-f1" n="8" xml:id="d544-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d544-f2" n="9" xml:id="d544-f2-content">
                <p>Dahl was never exchanged. He was finally released in February 1940 and returned
                    to the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
